<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Server\Vehicles\Models;

/**
 * Which model, textures, size and wheels each vehicle is drawn from.
 *
 * Read out of the game's own vehicle scripts under
 * media/scripts/generated/vehicles, with `template!` inheritance
 * resolved -- most vehicles declare only their model and inherit the
 * shell texture and their wheel positions from a template.
 *
 * Generated rather than written by hand: there are 241 of them, and a
 * mismatch between a script name and its model shows up as a vehicle
 * that silently will not draw.
 *
 * The size is the model's own measured extent, scaled by the script's
 * `scale` -- 53 of them have a model file to measure. The rest fall
 * back to the script's `extents`, which is the physics collision box
 * and runs between 15 % small and 15 % large against a real body, so it
 * is a stand-in rather than a substitute.
 *
 * A burnt-out shell has no mask, because it carries no paint. Wheels
 * are a separate mesh in the game's own text format, placed at the
 * offsets recorded here.
 */
final class VehicleCatalogue
{
    /** The mesh every vehicle's wheels use. */
    public const WHEEL_MESH = 'Vehicles_Wheel.txt';

    public const WHEEL_TEXTURE = 'vehicle_wheel.png';

